entry.summary:
In this part, I am going to make a simple bump allocator that just allocates memory. 
The file created is called malloc_v1.c
Note: 
The clues I mention below were given to me by an AI assistant, used purely to guide my understanding of concepts and syntax. The entire code is written by me, referencing the official glibc documentation throughout.
I'm mentioning this explicitly because I believe in being honest about the learning process.
The entire process and my code has been uploaded on my github account: [https://github.com/moonlitpath1/mini-malloc]
Create mymalloc.c. You need **two* functions (not one):*
#include <unistd.h>
#include <stddef.h>

